FL2000 for Ubuntu 26.04
======================

The supported target is amd64 with Linux 7.0. DKMS skips other kernel
series and architectures. Install headers matching every target kernel.
The package includes the checksum-pinned DRM helpers needed by Ubuntu's
kernel configuration, so DKMS does not download source during rebuilds.

Both fl2000 and the adapted it66121 module must be used. DKMS installs
these in updates/dkms; it does not overwrite distribution module files.
The adapted it66121 takes precedence over any same-named stock module.
It is not a validated replacement on native OF bridge boards. A built-in
stock IT66121 driver cannot be replaced by DKMS.

Install fl2000-enumerator for automatic discovery after connecting the
adapter. It uses /etc/fl2000/enumerator.conf, a udev rule, and an instance
of fl2000-enumerate@.service. Installation does not force-load the modules
or start enumeration for already connected devices; reconnect the adapter.
The kernel modules are autoloaded through ordinary USB/I2C device aliases.

Secure Boot uses the distribution's DKMS signing mechanism. Enroll the
local signing certificate when prompted; a PPA's archive signature does
not grant trust to locally built kernel modules.

Disconnect the adapter before removing or upgrading the driver. Package
removal does not unload modules still in use. Reconnect after installation
or reboot to ensure the installed versions are running. Removing the
package removes its DKMS modules and restores normal stock-module lookup.
Purge fl2000-enumerator to remove its configuration file.
